%>
<%
  page_data(
    title: "Revoking authorisation",
    error: false,
    caption: "API developer documentation",
    caption_size: 'l'
  )
%>

<p class="govuk-body">
You can revoke authorisation, for example if an access token has been leaked. You can do this using the API, or an appropriate body user can do it by signing in to the Register early career teachers service.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Revoking an access token using the API</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
To revoke an access token, send an HTTP POST request to our revoke endpoint.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
You must authenticate the request using <%= govuk_link_to("HTTP Basic Authentication", "https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7617/") %>
with your client ID and client secret.  To do this, add an HTTP header containing your credentials in the form <code>client_id:client_secret</code>, Base64 encoded.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
For example, if your client ID is <code>client123</code> and your secret is <code>supersecretvalue</code>, your Basic Authentication header would be:
</p>

<pre>
<code>
Authorization: Basic Y2xpZW50MTIzOnN1cGVyc2VjcmV0dmFsdWU=
</code>
</pre>


<%= govuk_warning_text(text: "Do not include your client ID or client secret in the body of the request.") %>

<p class="govuk-body">
Put the <code>token</code> parameter in the request body, not in additional request headers.
</p>

<%= govuk_table do |table|
  table.with_head do |head|
    head.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Parameter")
      row.with_cell(text: "Description")
    end
  end
  table.with_body do |body|
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell { tag.code("token") }
      row.with_cell(text: "The access token you want to revoke")
    end
  end
end %>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Example request</h3>

<pre>
<code>
curl -X POST <%= @api_base_url %>/oauth/revoke \
--user "client123:supersecretvalue" \
-H "content-type:application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
--data "token=[ACCESS-TOKEN-TO-REVOKE]"
</code>
</pre>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Response</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">
If the request is successful, we return HTTP status 200 with an empty body. The access token will no longer work.
</p>


<h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Error responses</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">
If the request is unsuccessful, we return an HTTP error status and a JSON payload containing an error value. For example: 
</p>

<pre>
<code>
{
  error: "invalid_client"
}
</code>
</pre>

<%= govuk_table do |table|
  table.with_head do |head|
    head.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Error scenario")
      row.with_cell(text: "HTTP status")
      row.with_cell(text: "Error code")
    end
  end
  table.with_body do |body|
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Client ID or client secret is invalid")
      row.with_cell(text: "401 (Unauthorized)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_client")
    end
  end
end %>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Removing access as an appropriate body user</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
The <strong>Manage data access</strong> page lists the applications that have access to send the appropriate body’s data to DfE.
</p>

<%= image_tag("documentation/authorisation/manage-data-access.png", width: "650px", alt: "Manage data access screen", class: "govuk-!-margin-top-2 govuk-!-margin-bottom-6") %>

<p class="govuk-body">
To remove an application’s access, select <strong>Remove access</strong> next to it.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
You’ll then be asked to confirm.
</p>

<%= image_tag("documentation/authorisation/confirm-remove-access.png", width: "650px", alt: "Confirm removal of access screen", class: "govuk-!-margin-top-2 govuk-!-margin-bottom-6") %>


<p class="govuk-body">
Select <strong>Confirm remove access</strong>.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
You’ll see a confirmation page. The application will no longer be able to access any of your data.
</p>

<%= image_tag("documentation/authorisation/access-removed.png", width: "650px", alt: "Access removed screen", class: "govuk-!-margin-top-2 govuk-!-margin-bottom-6") %>

